    {
      "id": "e7d5et2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Magnetism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bzfqrd0",
      "content": "Magnetism is the property of materials that attract iron and other magnetic materials."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ylmdwyp",
      "content": "Magnets have two poles: North pole and South pole."
    },
    {
      "id": "2l4yhat",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Properties of Magnets"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wdjfay5",
      "content": "• Like poles repel each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "byxo8if",
      "content": "• Unlike poles attract each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dzqtau9",
      "content": "• Magnetic poles always exist in pairs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "umu1mqi",
      "content": "• Magnetic force is strongest at the poles."
    },
    {
      "id": "c7hd6sl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Electromagnet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5nuiwfp",
      "content": "An electromagnet is a magnet produced by passing electric current through a coil of wire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "89mt425",
      "content": "Applications:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "An Ammeter is always connected in series due to low resistance, while a Voltmeter is connected in parallel due to high resistance.",
        "In a series circuit, current remains constant; in a parallel circuit, voltage remains constant across all branches.",
        "Fuse wire is made of an alloy with a low melting point and high resistance to protect circuits from overcurrent."
      ],
      "id": "lwdp2x7"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "59xio55",
      "content": "• Electric bell"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "u6sxki3",
      "content": "• Electric motors"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "95pl348",
      "content": "• Magnetic cranes"
    },
    {
      "id": "ogfn022",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "33oqnhe",
      "content": "• SI unit of electric current is Ampere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3rqaxdq",
      "content": "• Ohm’s law formula is V = IR."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cabntuf",
      "content": "• SI unit of resistance is Ohm."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4rfra2v",
      "content": "• Like poles repel and unlike poles attract."
    }
  ],
